*
* START-HISTORY:
* 1 Nov 26 dm   S.90 stage 3: N asks the id and hands the terminal to the IDE on a new item, shown as the dictionary form; ask.d, ask.i, show.new and write.item (the page's only write) and the
*               answer rules only they used are gone, so the page writes nothing: the dict-edit gate and the write are the IDE's.
* 31 Oct 26 dm  The A and S dictionary item types are gone (owner, 30 Oct 2026): N offers a data or a computed item only, C compiles and T tries D and I items, an index is offered on a D or I
*               item, and an old A or S item is shown with a sentence that says SD no longer reads it (its fields are not shown: they were in the Pick layout, which no program reads now).
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L2: the two boxes are panes of the layout service ($tk_layout): at 140 by 43 exactly the boxes the page has always drawn, in a bigger window the list shows more rows and the
*               description more lines, both wider; text longer than its box is wrapped when the box is wider than it was.  S.88 stage C: E hands the item to the IDE ('ide dict file item';
*               the IDE locks the record, asks the account's dict-edit gate and gives the lock back) and LIST.INDEX's hand-over is checked against 'ide list.index', in place of SED.
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.87: the page no longer names C among the types it compiles, tries or indexes (the messages now say A, S and I; D, A, S and I; A, S or I).
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.87: the C dictionary item type is gone: dcomp says message 12998 and makes no object code; the other programs no longer treat a C item as an I-type.
* 27 Oct 26 dm  S.87 batch 12: the dead FL$TYPE.SH branch of the file kind is gone with the constant.
* 27 Oct 26 dm  S.87 batch 4: the describe page no longer says a location of 9998 or 9999 shows the item count or the record length.
* 25 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 26 Oct 26 dm  faults: the record write's box says "Write this record?" (a sixth argument of $tk_confirm); the choice of keeping the page's own K$EDIT.OK question as the wall is written at write.item.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 2: the AI line ($tk_aipage), as tool.voc has it: F6 or AI > Ask the AI; the Items and Indices views, back to the file, filter and refresh are offered
*               to the model, and a proposal is carried out by the page's own key.  An account without the AI sees the page as it was.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 4 (the owner's editing actions): New and Compile are offered too, marked 'edit' (Enter alone rejects the proposal); the AI's argument is the DEFAULT of the
*               page's own prompt (the new item's id, a filter's text), checked as a typed answer, and every box after it applies.
* 8 Nov 26 dm   S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring'): Items, Indices and the AI line (the Files view and the AI line); Tab no longer
