* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse and Ctrl-O (the log of the commands run), the same on every page (the cases act:std.mouse and ctrl-o, through $tk_std).
* 10 Nov 26 dm  S.205: F11 is no longer the filter's second key: a terminal keeps it for its own full screen, and / is the key the page shows.
* 10 Nov 26 dm  S.138: a line longer than its box is wrapped at every width; it used to be cut at the reference width.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.DICT {file}     (in every account's VOC)
*
*   A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43 lines at least), for the dictionary of one data file of the account the session is in.  With a file named after the verb the page
*   opens that file's dictionary; with none it first lists the files the account's VOC points at (the VOC entries of type F) and Enter opens the dictionary of the one under the cursor.
*   THE ITEMS PANE lists every item of the dictionary: its id, its type (D data, I, E, L, PH, X; any other, an old A or S item included, is shown as its first character), where its value comes from (the field
*   number, or "computed"), its heading, format, conversion, whether it is single or multivalued, its association, and the expression of an I-type.  The box under the list describes the item
*   under the cursor in plain words.  THE INDICES PANE (I or Tab) lists the alternate key indices of the file: the item each is on, whether it is built, nulls, case, sort.
*
*   WHAT IT CAN DO.  THE PAGE WRITES NOTHING (S.90 stage 3, 1 Nov 2026).  N makes an item: the page asks the id and checks it, and hands the terminal to the IDE on a NEW item (ide dict file id),
*   which shows the dictionary form - the type, then the fields that type needs, each checked - and writes the record itself, with the account's dict-edit gate and the IDE's own questions.  E hands
*   the terminal to the IDE on the item that is there (ide dict file item) in the same way.  D deletes the item with the DELETE verb, after its id is typed.  C compiles an I item with
*   COMPILE.DICT.  T tries the item on a record of the data file: the value ITYPE() gives for that record, which is what the query processor computes, and the same value converted and formatted as
*   a query would print it.  In the indices pane N makes an index (CREATE.INDEX defines it, then BUILD.INDEX builds it, because an index that is not built finds nothing), B builds it again (BUILD.INDEX),
*   D deletes it (DELETE.INDEX, after its name is typed) and L lists it in full (LIST.INDEX: it prints to the terminal, which is handed to the verb).  Every verb is the one the person could type,
*   run through $tk_run after a box that shows the exact command and what it does; Cancel is the default.  An id or an index name with a character the page does not give to a command (a capital, a
*   dollar, an at sign) is listed and described, and the verb for it is typed at the prompt.
*
*   NO FILE IS HELD OPEN: every file the page opens (the dictionary, the data file) is closed again before the next key, because BUILD.INDEX and DELETE.INDEX need the file to themselves, and the
*   session's own open counts.
*
*   Keys: Up and Down, PgUp and PgDn, Home and End move; Enter opens a file (files pane); N, E, D, C, T, I and F (another file) in the items pane; N, B, D, L and I or Tab (back to the items) in the
*   indices pane; / filters by a part of the id; Esc clears the filter; F5 reads again; F1 or ? or a click on [?] explains the page; Ctrl-Q leaves.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_dict
$catalog $tool_dict

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h
$include dictdict.h

   prompt ''

   deffun edit_msg(kind) calling '!edit_msg'

   allow = 'delete compile.dict create.index build.index delete.index'   ;* the commands this page may run, through $tk_run, after a box
   show.allow = 'ide list.index'                                       ;* the two it hands the terminal to (the IDE is a screen; LIST.INDEX prints through the print unit)

   fa = downcase(field(trim(@sentence), ' ', 2))                       ;* the file named after the verb, if any

   call $tk_open('tool.dict', '', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'enter', 'open', 'open', 'Files', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'n', 'new', 'new', 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'e', 'edit', 'edit', 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'delete', 'delete', 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'c', 'compile', 'compile', 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 't', 'test', 'test', 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'i', 'indices', 'indices', 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f', 'file', 'file', 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'n', 'new index', 'newindex', 'Indices', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'b', 'build', 'build', 'Indices', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'd', 'delete', 'delindex', 'Indices', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'l', 'list', 'listindex', 'Indices', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'i', 'items', 'items', 'Indices', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '/', 'filter', 'filter', 'Files' : @sm : 'Items', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'read', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f6', 'box', 'nextpane', 'Items' : @sm : 'Indices', 1)     ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 move between the boxes on every page (the Files view has one: the AI line's own row names F6 there)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', 'Files' : @sm : 'Items', 1)       ;* S.88 U8: Esc takes the name filter of the pane off first, else opens the menu bar (in Indices it goes back to the items)
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'open', '&File', '&Open the file', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'new', '&Items', '&New item', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'edit', '&Items', '&Edit in the IDE', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'delete', '&Items', '&Delete', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'compile', '&Items', '&Compile', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'test', '&Items', '&Try the item', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'indices', '&Items', '&Indices', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'file', '&Items', 'Back to the &file', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'newindex', 'In&dex', '&New index', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'build', 'In&dex', '&Build', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'delindex', 'In&dex', '&Delete the index', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'listindex', 'In&dex', '&List', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'items', 'In&dex', 'I&tems', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'filter', '&View', '&Filter the names', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', '&Refresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'nextpane', '&View', '&Next box', '', '')     ;* S.180: every key's action is on a menu (F6)
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this page', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   * S.97 stage 2: the AI line.  The page offers the AI only the actions that change what is shown - the Items and Indices views, back to the file, the filter and refresh (the
   * owner: opt-in, off by default); a proposal is carried out by the page's own key.  Where the AI is not usable for the account nothing here adds a key, a row or a line.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'indices', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'items', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'file', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'filter', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'new', 'edit', '', '', '')                ;* S.97 stage 4 (the owner's editing actions): a new item, its id the AI's argument; Reject is the default
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'compile', 'edit', '', '', '')            ;* and compile the I item under the cursor, through the page's own Run box
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   VIS = 16                                                            ;* rows of a list on the screen (the list pane's height less 6: set by get.rects)
   MAXV = 3000                                                        ;* items read: a dictionary is some tens; more than this are not listed, and the page says so
   hl.f = fmt('File', '30L') : fmt('Kind', '12L') : fmt('Dictionary', '12L') : fmt('Items', '8R') : fmt('Indices', '9R')
   hl.i = fmt('Id', '26L') : fmt('Type', '5L') : fmt('Field', '9L') : fmt('Heading', '22L') : fmt('Format', '8L') : fmt('Conversion', '12L') : fmt('S/M', '4L') : fmt('Association', '12L') : 'Expression or text'
   hl.x = fmt('Index', '24L') : fmt('Built', '6L') : fmt('Type', '5L') : fmt('Nulls', '6L') : fmt('S/M', '5L') : fmt('Fmt', '5L') : fmt('Case', '6L') : 'Field or expression'

   ctl.set = ''                                                        ;* the characters that are never shown as they are (controls, DEL and the bytes above ASCII)
   for cq = 1 to 31
      ctl.set := char(cq)
   next cq
   for cq = 127 to 255
      ctl.set := char(cq)
   next cq
   ctl.rep = str('.', len(ctl.set))

   pi = 1                                                              ;* the pane: 1 files, 2 items, 3 indices
   pnames = 'Files' : @fm : 'Items' : @fm : 'Indices'
   fnames = '' ; fmeta = '' ; nf = 0 ; fshown = '' ; nfs = 0
   iids = '' ; imeta = '' ; ni = 0 ; ishown = '' ; nis = 0
   xnames = '' ; xmeta = '' ; nx = 0
   cf = 1 ; ci = 1 ; cx = 1 ; tf = 0 ; ti = 0 ; tx = 0
   filtf = '' ; filti = ''
   fn = '' ; truncated = 0 ; lastrec = '' ; pre.item = ''
   gen = 0
   done = 0
   msg = ''

   perr = ''
   gosub declare.layout
   gosub read.files
   if fa # '' then
      gosub open.named
   end else
      msg = 'Up and Down move; Enter opens the dictionary of the file under the cursor'
   end
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, pnames<pi>, '', '', mr)           ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole, and the frame then writes the app name at its right end
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, pnames<pi>, msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pi>, nm, ao)          ;* S.97 stage 2: while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys, before the bar sees them
      ai.arg = ''                                                                    ;* S.97 stage 4: the argument of an accepted proposal, the DEFAULT of this page's own prompt for that key
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted: this page's own key for it
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then ai.arg = ao<5>
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      busy = (if (pi = 1 and filtf # '') or (pi = 2 and filti # '') or pi = 3 then 1 else 0)
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, pnames<pi>, nm, busy, mr)       ;* the Esc rule: the pane's name filter is taken off before the bar opens, and Esc in the Indices pane goes back to the items (key.indices)
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page: all of it is drawn again
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', chg)
            gosub get.rects
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the system says

* Every file of the account (the VOC entries of type F) with its kind, whether it has a dictionary, how many items, how many indices; the cursor goes back to the file it was on
read.files:
   sel.f = ''
   if nfs > 0 and cf >= 1 and cf <= nfs then sel.f = fnames<fshown<cf>>
   fnames = ''
   fmeta = ''
   open 'VOC' to vocf then
      sselect vocf to 9
      readlist ids from 9 else ids = ''
      n = dcount(ids, @fm)
      if ids = '' then n = 0
      for i = 1 to n
         read r from vocf, ids<i> then
            * the first field is F, or a description that starts "File" (a file's description is kept there)
            t1 = upcase(r<1>)
            if t1 = 'F' or t1[1, 5] = 'FILE ' then fnames<-1> = ids<i>
         end
      next i
      close vocf
   end
   nf = dcount(fnames, @fm)
   if fnames = '' then nf = 0
   for i = 1 to nf
      fn2 = fnames<i>
      gosub read.fmeta
      fmeta<i> = meta
   next i
   gosub apply.filter.f
   if sel.f # '' then
      for i = 1 to nfs
         if fnames<fshown<i>> = sel.f then
            cf = i
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   if cf > nfs then cf = nfs
   if cf < 1 then cf = 1
   return

* In: fn2.  Out: meta, a field of values: kind, dictionary (1 or 0), items, indices.  Every file opened here is closed again.
read.fmeta:
   meta = ''
   kind = 'cannot open' ; dct = 0 ; nitems = '' ; nidx = ''
   open fn2 to fv then
      ft = fileinfo(fv, FL$TYPE)
      begin case
         case ft = FL$TYPE.DH
            kind = 'dynamic'
         case ft = FL$TYPE.DIR
            kind = 'directory'
         case ft = FL$TYPE.SEQ
            kind = 'sequential'
         case ft = FL$TYPE.NET
            kind = 'server'
         case 1
            kind = 'other'
      end case
      if ft = FL$TYPE.DH then
         ixl = indices(fv)
         nidx = dcount(ixl, @fm)
         if ixl = '' then nidx = 0
      end
      close fv
      open 'DICT', fn2 to dv then
         dct = 1
         nitems = fileinfo(dv, FL$RECORD.COUNT)
         close dv
      end
   end
   meta = kind : @vm : dct : @vm : nitems : @vm : nidx
   return

apply.filter.f:
   fshown = ''
   nfs = 0
   fu = upcase(filtf)
   for q = 1 to nf
      if filtf = '' or index(upcase(fnames<q>), fu, 1) > 0 then
         fshown<-1> = q
         nfs += 1
      end
   next q
   return

* The items of the dictionary of fn, in id order, with what the list shows of each; the cursor goes back to the item it was on
read.items:
   sel.i = ''
   if nis > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nis then sel.i = iids<ishown<ci>>
   iids = '' ; imeta = '' ; truncated = 0
   open 'DICT', fn to dv then
      sselect dv to 9
      readlist ids from 9 else ids = ''
      n = dcount(ids, @fm)
      if ids = '' then n = 0
      if n > MAXV then
         n = MAXV
         truncated = 1
      end
      for i = 1 to n
         read rec from dv, ids<i> then
            gosub classify.item
            iids<-1> = ids<i>
            imeta<-1> = ty : @vm : wh : @vm : hd : @vm : ft2 : @vm : cv : @vm : sm : @vm : asoc : @vm : ex
         end
      next i
      close dv
   end
   ni = dcount(iids, @fm)
   if iids = '' then ni = 0
   gosub apply.filter.i
   if sel.i # '' then
      for i = 1 to nis
         if iids<ishown<i>> = sel.i then
            ci = i
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   if ci > nis then ci = nis
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   return

apply.filter.i:
   ishown = ''
   nis = 0
   fu = upcase(filti)
   for q = 1 to ni
      if filti = '' or index(upcase(iids<q>), fu, 1) > 0 then
         ishown<-1> = q
         nis += 1
      end
   next q
   return

* In: rec (an item).  Out: ty (D data, E, I, L, PH, X or any other first character, an old A or S included), wh (where the value comes from), hd (heading), ft2 (format), cv (conversion), sm (S or M),
* asoc (association), ex (expression or text).  Every one is cleaned for the screen.
classify.item:
   ty = upcase(rec<DICT.TYPE>)
   if ty[1, 2] = 'PH' then ty = 'PH' else ty = ty[1, 1]
   wh = '' ; hd = '' ; ft2 = '' ; cv = '' ; sm = '' ; asoc = '' ; ex = ''
   begin case
      case ty = 'D' or ty = 'E'
         wh = rec<DICT.LOC> ; cv = rec<DICT.CONV> ; hd = rec<DICT.DISPLAY.NAME> ; ft2 = rec<DICT.FORMAT> ; sm = rec<DICT.S.M> ; asoc = rec<DICT.ASSOC>
      case ty = 'I'
         wh = 'computed' ; ex = rec<DICT.ITYPE.SOURCE> ; cv = rec<DICT.CONV> ; hd = rec<DICT.DISPLAY.NAME> ; ft2 = rec<DICT.FORMAT> ; sm = rec<DICT.S.M> ; asoc = rec<DICT.ASSOC>
      case ty = 'L'
         wh = 'link' ; ex = rec<2> : '  file ' : rec<3>
      case ty = 'X' or ty = 'PH'
         ex = rec<2>
   end case
   ct = wh ; gosub clean.text ; wh = ct
   ct = hd ; gosub clean.text ; hd = ct
   ct = ft2 ; gosub clean.text ; ft2 = ct
   ct = cv ; gosub clean.text ; cv = ct
   ct = sm ; gosub clean.text ; sm = ct
   ct = asoc ; gosub clean.text ; asoc = ct
   ct = ex ; gosub clean.text ; ex = ct
   ct = ty ; gosub clean.text ; ty = ct
   return

* In/out: ct.  The text as the screen may show it: value and subvalue marks become | and \, and every control character, DEL and byte above ASCII becomes a dot
clean.text:
   ct = convert(@vm, '|', ct)
   ct = convert(@sm, '\', ct)
   ct = convert(ctl.set, ctl.rep, ct)
   return

* The alternate key indices of the file fn: for each its name and what the file says about it.  The file is opened only for this and closed again, so that a build can have it to itself.
read.indices:
   sel.x = ''
   if nx > 0 and cx >= 1 and cx <= nx then sel.x = xnames<cx>
   xnames = '' ; xmeta = ''
   open fn to fv then
      ixl = indices(fv)
      for i = 1 to dcount(ixl, @fm)
         if ixl<i> # '' then
            dd = indices(fv, ixl<i>)
            xt = upcase(dd<1, 1>)
            if xt = '' then xt = 'D'
            xs = dd<6>                                                ;* single or multivalued
            xj = dd<5>                                                ;* L or R: how the keys are justified, which is how they are ordered
            ct = dd<2> ; gosub clean.text
            xnames<-1> = ixl<i>
            xmeta<-1> = (if dd<1, 4> = '1' then 'yes' else 'no') : @vm : xt : @vm : (if dd<1, 3> = '1' then 'no' else 'yes') : @vm : xs : @vm : xj : @vm : (if dd<1, 8> = '1' then 'any' else 'exact') : @vm : ct
         end
      next i
      close fv
   end
   nx = dcount(xnames, @fm)
   if xnames = '' then nx = 0
   if sel.x # '' then
      for i = 1 to nx
         if xnames<i> = sel.x then
            cx = i
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   if cx > nx then cx = nx
   if cx < 1 then cx = 1
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the file the page works on

* The file named after the verb: a name of a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore that is one of the account's files and has a dictionary
open.named:
   cw = fa
   gosub check.word
   if not(okname) then
      msg = 'a file name is made of a-z, 0-9, dot, dash and underscore only: pick the file from the list'
      return
   end
   found = 0
   for q = 1 to nf
      if upcase(fnames<q>) = upcase(fa) then
         found = q
         exit
      end
   next q
   if not(found) then
      msg = fa : ' is not a file in this account: pick one from the list'
      return
   end
   fn = fnames<found>
   gosub enter.file
   return

* In: fn.  The dictionary of fn is opened to see that it is there; then the items are read and the items pane is shown
enter.file:
   dictok = 0
   open 'DICT', fn to dv then
      dictok = 1
      close dv
   end
   if not(dictok) then
      msg = fn : ' has no dictionary: there is nothing to show (a file made by create.file has one)'
      fn = ''
      return
   end
   pi = 2
   ci = 1 ; ti = 0 ; filti = ''
   iids = '' ; imeta = '' ; ni = 0 ; ishown = '' ; nis = 0
   gosub read.items
   msg = ''
   if truncated then msg = 'the dictionary has more than ' : MAXV : ' items: the first ' : MAXV : ' are listed'
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

* The layout (S.88 L2).  The two boxes are panes of the layout service, declared in the sizes of the reference layout (140 by 43, the body 138 by 39): the list stretches (a bigger window
* shows more rows of the files, items or indices), the description takes the columns.  The same two panes serve the three views of the page.
* Out: lx ly lw lh (the list), dx dy dw dh (the description), tw (the text width of both), VIS (the rows of a list).
declare.layout:
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'list' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 22 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<2> = 'detail' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 17 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, perr)
   gosub get.rects
   return

get.rects:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'list', rc)
   lx = rc<1, 1> ; ly = rc<1, 2> ; lw = rc<1, 3> ; lh = rc<1, 4>
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, 'detail', rc)
   dx = rc<1, 1> ; dy = rc<1, 2> ; dw = rc<1, 3> ; dh = rc<1, 4>
   tw = lw - 4
   VIS = lh - 6                                                        ;* the header row, the rows, the two summary lines, a blank row and the border: 16 rows of 22
   return

* In: lines.  Out: dlines, what the description shows.  A line longer than the box is wrapped at its width (S.138).
fit.lines:
   dlines = lines
   if lines # '' then
      dlines = ''
      nd = 0
      for q = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
         nd += 1
         dlines<nd> = ''
         if lines<q> # '' then
            call $tk_wrap(lines<q>, tw, wpieces)
            for pj = 1 to dcount(wpieces, @fm)
               dlines<nd> = wpieces<pj>
               nd += 1
            next pj
            nd -= 1
         end
      next q
   end
   return

draw.all:
   screen clear at 0,ctx<TK.C.YBODY> size ctx<TK.C.W>,ctx<TK.C.BODYH>
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         ttl = 'Files of ' : @who
         btl = 'The file under the cursor'
      case pi = 2
         ttl = 'Dictionary of ' : fn
         btl = 'The item under the cursor'
      case 1
         ttl = 'Indices of ' : fn
         btl = 'The index under the cursor'
   end case
   screen box at lx,ly size lw,lh title ttl
   screen box at dx,dy size dw,dh title btl
   gosub draw.list
   gosub draw.detail
   return

* In: pi.  Out: cp (the cursor), cn (rows), tp (the first row shown)
load.cur:
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         cp = cf ; cn = nfs ; tp = tf
      case pi = 2
         cp = ci ; cn = nis ; tp = ti
      case 1
         cp = cx ; cn = nx ; tp = tx
   end case
   return

store.cur:
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         cf = cp ; tf = tp
      case pi = 2
         ci = cp ; ti = tp
      case 1
         cx = cp ; tx = tp
   end case
   return

draw.list:
   gosub load.cur
   if cp <= tp then tp = cp - 1
   if cp > tp + VIS then tp = cp - VIS
   if tp > cn - VIS then tp = cn - VIS                                 ;* a taller list fills its rows again
   if tp < 0 then tp = 0
   gosub store.cur
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         screen text hl.f at lx + 2,ly + 1 attr 'header' width tw
      case pi = 2
         screen text hl.i at lx + 2,ly + 1 attr 'header' width tw
      case 1
         screen text hl.x at lx + 2,ly + 1 attr 'header' width tw
   end case
   for r = 1 to VIS
      kk = tp + r
      s = ''
      if kk <= cn then
         begin case
            case pi = 1
               s = fmt(fnames<fshown<kk>>, '30L')
               ma = fmeta<fshown<kk>>
               s := fmt(ma<1, 1>, '12L') : fmt((if ma<1, 2> = 1 then 'yes' else 'none'), '12L') : fmt(ma<1, 3>, '8R') : fmt(ma<1, 4>, '9R')
            case pi = 2
               ma = imeta<ishown<kk>>
               s = fmt(iids<ishown<kk>>, '26L') : fmt(ma<1, 1>, '5L') : fmt(ma<1, 2>, '9L') : fmt(ma<1, 3>, '22L') : fmt(ma<1, 4>, '8L') : fmt(ma<1, 5>, '12L') : fmt(ma<1, 6>, '4L') : fmt(ma<1, 7>, '12L') : ma<1, 8>
            case 1
               ma = xmeta<kk>
               s = fmt(xnames<kk>, '24L') : fmt(ma<1, 1>, '6L') : fmt(ma<1, 2>, '5L') : fmt(ma<1, 3>, '6L') : fmt(ma<1, 4>, '5L') : fmt(ma<1, 5>, '5L') : fmt(ma<1, 6>, '6L') : ma<1, 7>
         end case
      end
      screen text s at lx + 2,ly + 1 + r attr (if kk = cp and kk <= cn then 'highlight' else 'normal') width tw
   next r
   gosub draw.foot
   call $tk_help('mark', lx + lw - 5, ly + 1, 0, 0)
   return

* The summary under the list, and the dict-edit gate this session holds (asked of the kernel, never tried)
draw.foot:
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         s = nf : (if nf = 1 then ' file' else ' files')
         if filtf # '' then s := ', ' : nfs : ' with "' : filtf : '" in the name'
      case pi = 2
         s = ni : (if ni = 1 then ' item' else ' items')
         if filti # '' then s := ', ' : nis : ' with "' : filti : '" in the id'
         if truncated then s := ' (the first ' : MAXV : ')'
      case 1
         s = nx : (if nx = 1 then ' index' else ' indices')
   end case
   gadm = kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1)                           ;* the verbs let the administrator through whatever the bit says (P3)
   s := '.   Your gate:  dict-edit ' : (if gadm then 'on (administrator)' else (if kernel(K$DICT.EDIT, -1) then 'on' else 'off'))
   screen text fmt(s, tw : 'L') at lx + 2,ly + lh - 4 attr 'bold' width tw
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         s2 = 'Enter opens the dictionary of the file under the cursor.  A file can also be named after the verb: tool.dict customers'
      case pi = 2
         s2 = 'N writes a new item itself, only if dict-edit is on.  E, D and C run the IDE and the verbs, which make their own checks.  T tries an item on a record.'
      case 1
         s2 = 'An index that is not built finds nothing: B builds it.  Build and delete need the file to themselves: another session having it open refuses them.'
   end case
   wpieces = s2
   call $tk_wrap(s2, tw, wpieces)
   screen text fmt(wpieces<1>, tw : 'L') at lx + 2,ly + lh - 3 width tw
   if wpieces<2> # '' then screen text fmt(wpieces<2>, tw : 'L') at lx + 2,ly + lh - 2 width tw
   return

draw.detail:
   lines = ''
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         if nfs >= 1 and cf >= 1 and cf <= nfs then
            gosub describe.file
         end else
            lines<-1> = (if nf = 0 then 'This account has no files.' else 'No file name holds "' : filtf : '".  Esc shows all of them.')
         end
      case pi = 2
         if nis >= 1 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nis then
            gosub describe.item
         end else
            lines<-1> = (if ni = 0 then 'This dictionary has no items.  N makes one.' else 'No item id holds "' : filti : '".  Esc shows all of them.')
         end
      case 1
         if nx >= 1 and cx >= 1 and cx <= nx then
            gosub describe.index
         end else
            lines<-1> = 'This file has no indices.  N makes one on an item of the dictionary.'
         end
   end case
   gosub fit.lines
   for r = 1 to dh - 2
      screen text fmt(dlines<r>[1, tw], tw : 'L') at dx + 2,dy + r width tw
   next r
   return

* The file under the cursor: where it is, its dictionary, its indices
describe.file:
   fn2 = fnames<fshown<cf>>
   ma = fmeta<fshown<cf>>
   lines<-1> = fn2 : '  -  a ' : ma<1, 1> : ' file'
   open fn2 to fv then
      lines<-1> = 'Data: ' : fileinfo(fv, FL$PATH)
      close fv
   end else
      lines<-1> = 'The VOC points at a file this account cannot open now.'
   end
   if ma<1, 2> = 1 then
      open 'DICT', fn2 to dv then
         lines<-1> = 'Dictionary: ' : fileinfo(dv, FL$PATH) : '  (about ' : ma<1, 3> : ' items)'
         close dv
      end
      lines<-1> = 'Enter opens it.'
   end else
      lines<-1> = 'This file has no dictionary: a query cannot read it by field name.'
   end
   if ma<1, 4> # '' and ma<1, 4> > 0 then
      lines<-1> = 'Indices: ' : ma<1, 4> : ' (the indices pane of its dictionary lists them)'
   end
   return

* In: the item under the cursor.  Out: lines, the description in sentences
describe.item:
   iid = iids<ishown<ci>>
   lines<-1> = ''
   rec = ''
   open 'DICT', fn to dv then
      read rec from dv, iid else rec = ''
      close dv
   end
   if rec = '' then
      lines<1> = iid : '  -  this item is not in the dictionary now (F5 reads it again)'
      return
   end
   gosub classify.item
   gosub type.words
   lines<1> = iid : '  -  ' : tyw
   loc = wh
   begin case
      case ty = 'D'
         if loc = '' or not(num(loc)) then
            lines<-1> = 'Its location "' : loc : '" is not a field number, so a query cannot read it.'
         end else
            begin case
               case loc = 0
                  lines<-1> = 'Shows the record id.'
               case 1
                  lines<-1> = 'Shows field ' : loc : ' of each record.'
            end case
         end
      case ty = 'I'
         lines<-1> = 'Computes its value for each record from the expression:'
         ct = ex
         call $tk_wrap(ct, tw - 6, pieces)
         for pq = 1 to dcount(pieces, @fm)
            if pq <= 3 then lines<-1> = '    ' : pieces<pq>
         next pq
         if rec<DICT.SYS.INFO> # '' and rec<DICT.ITYPE.OBJECT> # '' then
            lines<-1> = 'Compiled: the query processor runs the compiled form.'
         end else
            lines<-1> = 'Not compiled yet: C compiles it (a query compiles it when it first uses it).'
         end
      case ty = 'E'
         lines<-1> = 'Shows the element ' : wh : ' of each record of a data collection file.'
      case ty = 'L'
         lines<-1> = 'Names another file and how to find the record in it: ' : ex : '.'
      case ty = 'PH'
         lines<-1> = 'A phrase: a fragment of a query command, replaced where its name is typed: ' : ex
      case ty = 'X'
         lines<-1> = 'Text kept in the dictionary under this name.  A query does not read it as a field.'
      case ty = 'A' or ty = 'S'
         lines<-1> = 'SD no longer reads A and S items: a query that names it is refused.  Write it again as a data item (N, D) or a computed item (N, I).'
      case 1
         lines<-1> = 'SD reads this item as nothing a query can use.'
   end case
   if ty = 'D' or ty = 'I' or ty = 'E' then
      begin case
         case hd = ''
            lines<-1> = 'The column heading is the name of the item.'
         case hd = '\'
            lines<-1> = 'No column heading is printed.'
         case 1
            lines<-1> = 'Column heading "' : hd : '".'
      end case
      if ft2 = '' then
         lines<-1> = 'No format: SD takes ten characters, left-justified for text and right-justified for numbers.'
      end else
         fs = ft2
         gosub describe.format
         lines<-1> = 'Printed ' : fdesc : '.'
      end
      if cv = '' then
         lines<-1> = 'No conversion: the stored value is printed as it is.'
      end else
         cs = cv
         gosub describe.conv
         lines<-1> = 'Converted for display with ' : cv : ' (' : cdesc : ').'
      end
      begin case
         case sm = 'M'
            lines<-1> = 'Multivalued: the field holds several values.' : (if asoc # '' then '  Association ' : asoc : ': its values line up, value by value, with the other items of that association.' else '')
         case sm = 'S'
            lines<-1> = 'Single valued.' : (if asoc # '' then '  Association ' : asoc : '.' else '')
         case 1
            lines<-1> = 'Single or multivalued is not said.' : (if asoc # '' then '  Association ' : asoc : '.' else '')
      end case
   end
   lines<-1> = ''
   rawl = 'Record:'
   for rq = 1 to dcount(rec, @fm)
      if rq <= DICT.SYS.INFO - 1 then
         ct = rec<rq> ; gosub clean.text
         rawl := ' ' : rq : '=' : (if ct = '' then '-' else ct)
      end
   next rq
   call $tk_wrap(rawl, tw - 6, pieces)
   for pq = 1 to dcount(pieces, @fm)
      if pq <= 2 then lines<-1> = pieces<pq>
   next pq
   lines<-1> = 'E edits it in the IDE, T tries it on a record, C compiles it, D deletes it.'
   return

* In: ty.  Out: tyw, the type in words
type.words:
   begin case
      case ty = 'D'
         tyw = 'a data field (D)'
      case ty = 'A'
         tyw = 'an A-type item, which SD no longer reads (A)'
      case ty = 'S'
         tyw = 'an S-type item, which SD no longer reads (S)'
      case ty = 'I'
         tyw = 'a computed field (I-type)'
      case ty = 'E'
         tyw = 'an element of a data collection (E)'
      case ty = 'L'
         tyw = 'a link to another file (L)'
      case ty = 'PH'
         tyw = 'a phrase (PH)'
      case ty = 'X'
         tyw = 'text (X)'
      case 1
         tyw = 'an item of type "' : ty : '"'
   end case
   return

* In: fs (a format such as 10R2).  Out: fdesc, the format in words
describe.format:
   fdesc = ''
   fw = '' ; fq = 1
   loop while fq <= len(fs) and index('0123456789', fs[fq, 1], 1) > 0 do
      fw := fs[fq, 1]
      fq += 1
   repeat
   fj = upcase(fs[fq, 1])
   fq += 1
   fd = ''
   loop while fq <= len(fs) and index('0123456789', fs[fq, 1], 1) > 0 do
      fd := fs[fq, 1]
      fq += 1
   repeat
   fo = fs[fq, 99]
   if fw = '' or index('LRTCU', fj, 1) = 0 or fj = '' then
      fdesc = 'in the format "' : fs : '"'
      return
   end
   begin case
      case fj = 'L'
         jw = 'left-justified'
      case fj = 'R'
         jw = 'right-justified'
      case fj = 'T'
         jw = 'as text, wrapped at word breaks'
      case fj = 'C'
         jw = 'centered'
      case 1
         jw = 'left-justified, not trimmed'
   end case
   fdesc = fw : ' characters wide, ' : jw
   if fd # '' then fdesc := ', ' : fd : ' decimal places'
   if fo # '' then fdesc := ', with the options "' : fo : '"'
   return

* In: cs (a conversion code).  Out: cdesc, what kind of conversion it is
describe.conv:
   c1 = upcase(cs[1, 1])
   c2 = upcase(cs[1, 2])
   begin case
      case c2 = 'MD' or c2 = 'ML' or c2 = 'MR'
         cdesc = 'a number with decimal places'
      case c2 = 'MC'
         cdesc = 'a change of the characters'
      case c2 = 'MT'
         cdesc = 'a time'
      case c2 = 'MX' or c2 = 'MB' or c2 = 'MO'
         cdesc = 'hexadecimal, binary or octal'
      case c1 = 'D'
         cdesc = 'a date'
      case c1 = 'T'
         cdesc = 'a look-up in another file'
      case c1 = 'G'
         cdesc = 'a group taken out of the value'
      case c1 = 'U'
         cdesc = 'a subroutine of the account'
      case 1
         cdesc = 'a conversion code'
   end case
   return

* The index under the cursor in words
describe.index:
   xn = xnames<cx>
   ma = xmeta<cx>
   lines<-1> = xn : '  -  ' : (if ma<1, 1> = 'yes' then 'a built index: it finds records by the value of its field.' else 'defined but NOT BUILT: it finds nothing until B builds it from the records.')
   begin case
      case ma<1, 2> = 'I'
         lines<-1> = 'It is on the computed item with the expression: ' : ma<1, 7>
      case ma<1, 2> = 'A' or ma<1, 2> = 'S'
         lines<-1> = 'It was made from an A or S item, which SD no longer reads, so a query never uses it.  Delete it (D); N makes one on a data or computed item.'
      case 1
         lines<-1> = 'It is on field ' : ma<1, 7> : ' of each record.'
   end case
   lines<-1> = 'Records with an empty value are ' : (if ma<1, 3> = 'yes' then 'indexed.' else 'left out.') : '  Case: ' : (if ma<1, 6> = 'any' then 'differences of case do not matter.' else 'exact.') : '  Keys are ordered as ' : (if ma<1, 5> = 'R' then 'right-justified values (numbers by value).' else 'left-justified text.')
   lines<-1> = ''
   lines<-1> = 'N makes an index of an item (create.index defines it, then build.index builds it).  B builds this one again.  D deletes it.  L lists it in full.'
   lines<-1> = 'Build and delete need the file to themselves: if another session has it open, the verb says so and nothing changes.'
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 then nm = downcase(nm)                          ;* N and n are one key
   begin case
      case nm = 'up' or nm = 'down' or nm = 'pgup' or nm = 'pgdn' or nm = 'home' or nm = 'end'
         gosub move.cursor
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         call $tk_help('box', 'tool.dict.page', hm, 0, 0)
         if hm # '' then msg = hm
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* S.179: the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* S.186: the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* S.179: the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, pnames<pi>, std.r)
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub reread
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read again'
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         * S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 go round the boxes and the AI line: the Files view is one box; Items and Indices are two (Indices is where I and Tab used to take the focus)
         rg.n = (if pi = 1 then 1 else 2)
         rg.at = (if pi = 3 then 2 else 1)
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, rg.at, nm : @fm : rg.n, ap)
         msg = ap<2>
         begin case
            case rg.n = 1
               null                                                        ;* one box: the line took or gave back the focus, nothing of the page moves
            case ap<1> = 2 and pi = 2
               gosub to.indices
            case ap<1> = 1 and pi = 3
               pi = 2
               gosub draw.all
         end case
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
      case pi = 1
         gosub key.files
      case pi = 2
         gosub key.items
      case 1
         gosub key.indices
   end case
   return

move.cursor:
   gosub load.cur
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         if cp > 1 then cp -= 1
      case nm = 'down'
         if cp < cn then cp += 1
      case nm = 'pgup'
         cp -= VIS
         if cp < 1 then cp = 1
      case nm = 'pgdn'
         cp += VIS
         if cp > cn then cp = cn
      case nm = 'home'
         cp = 1
      case nm = 'end'
         if cn > 0 then cp = cn
   end case
   gosub store.cur
   gosub draw.all
   return

* F5: the pane's own data again
reread:
   begin case
      case pi = 1
         gosub read.files
      case pi = 2
         gosub read.items
      case 1
         gosub read.indices
   end case
   return

key.files:
   begin case
      case nm = 'enter'
         if nfs < 1 then return
         fn = fnames<fshown<cf>>
         gosub enter.file
         gosub draw.all
      case nm = '/'
         screen ask 'Part of a file name (empty shows every file)' width 40 value ai.arg title 'Filter' returning ft1 then got = 1 else got = 0
         if not(got) then return
         filtf = trim(ft1)
         gosub apply.filter.f
         cf = 1 ; tf = 0
         gosub draw.all
         msg = (if filtf = '' then 'every file' else nfs : ' with "' : filtf : '"')
      case nm = 'esc'
         if filtf # '' then
            filtf = ''
            gosub apply.filter.f
            cf = 1 ; tf = 0
            gosub draw.all
         end
   end case
   return

key.items:
   begin case
      case nm = 'esc'
         if filti # '' then
            filti = ''
            gosub apply.filter.i
            ci = 1 ; ti = 0
            gosub draw.all
         end
      case nm = 'n'
         gosub do.new
      case nm = 'e'
         gosub do.edit
      case nm = 'd'
         gosub do.delete
      case nm = 'c'
         gosub do.compile
      case nm = 't'
         gosub do.test
      case nm = 'i'
         gosub to.indices
      case nm = 'f'
         pi = 1
         gosub read.files
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'Enter opens the dictionary of the file under the cursor'
      case nm = '/'
         screen ask 'Part of an item id (empty shows every item)' width 40 value ai.arg title 'Filter' returning ft1 then got = 1 else got = 0
         if not(got) then return
         filti = trim(ft1)
         gosub apply.filter.i
         ci = 1 ; ti = 0
         gosub draw.all
         msg = (if filti = '' then 'every item' else nis : ' with "' : filti : '"')
   end case
   return

key.indices:
   begin case
      case nm = 'i' or nm = 'esc'
         pi = 2
         gosub draw.all
      case nm = 'n'
         gosub do.newindex
      case nm = 'b'
         gosub do.build
      case nm = 'd'
         gosub do.delindex
      case nm = 'l'
         gosub do.listindex
   end case
   return

* I or Tab: the indices pane; the item under the cursor is the one offered when N asks for the field
to.indices:
   pre.item = ''
   if nis >= 1 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nis then pre.item = iids<ishown<ci>>
   pi = 3
   cx = 1 ; tx = 0
   gosub read.indices
   gosub draw.all
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, pnames<pi>, mev, '', mr)                  ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key                          ;* a bar left with nothing chosen has no name: the status message stays
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, pnames<pi>, mev, ap)                         ;* S.97 stage 2: a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, lx + lw - 5, ly + 1, hit.m)
   if hit.m then
      call $tk_help('box', 'tool.dict.page', hm, 0, 0)
      if hm # '' then msg = hm
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      if mx >= lx + 2 and mx <= lx + lw - 3 and my >= ly + 2 and my <= ly + 1 + VIS then
         gosub load.cur
         if tp + my - ly - 1 <= cn then
            cp = tp + my - ly - 1
            gosub store.cur
            gosub draw.all
         end
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the page can run

* In: cw.  Out: okname.  A word the page may give to a command: letters a-z, digits, dot, dash and underscore only (what $tk_run lets through), at most 63 long
check.word:
   okname = (len(cw) > 0 and len(cw) <= 63)
   good = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-'
   for cwq = 1 to len(cw)
      if index(good, cw[cwq, 1], 1) = 0 then okname = @false
   next cwq
   if okname then
      * a word the VOC holds as a keyword (all, no.query, detail, lptr, data, dict, local ...) is read by the verb as that keyword, whoever's item or index it is: DELETE DICT file ALL asks to
      * delete every item and DELETE.INDEX file ALL removes every index, on a name the box and the typed name said was one
      open 'VOC' to kwf then
         read kwr from kwf, cw then
            if upcase(kwr<1>[1, 1]) = 'K' then okname = @false
         end
         close kwf
      end
   end
   return

* The lines the verb printed, in one line for the status bar
join.out:
   out = change(change(change(out, char(13) : char(10), @fm), char(10), @fm), char(13), '')
   said = ''
   for oi = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
      if trim(out<oi>) # '' then said := (if said = '' then '' else ' / ') : trim(out<oi>)
   next oi
   ct = said ; gosub clean.text ; said = ct[1, 220]               ;* the verb's words can echo an expression of the dictionary: no control character reaches the terminal
   return

* Run sent with the confirm box already answered Run: the verb's own words go to the status line
run.sent:
   call $tk_run(allow, sent, out, stat, rerr)
   if rerr # '' then
      msg = rerr
      return
   end
   gosub join.out
   msg = (if said # '' then said else sent : ' ran')
   return

* The terminal goes to a verb that shows a screen (the IDE) or prints a report (LIST.INDEX) and comes back: the page is taken again afterwards and what it lists is read again.  In: sent, keep (the
* id or index name to put the cursor on again).  Only the two verbs of show.allow can get here.
hand.over:
   if index(' ' : show.allow : ' ', ' ' : field(sent, ' ', 1) : ' ', 1) = 0 then
      msg = 'the page does not run ' : field(sent, ' ', 1)
      return
   end
   call $tk_close(ctx)
   execute sent
   crt
   crt sysmsg(12870) :                                         ;* Press Enter to return
   input junk
   if junk = char(1) then null                                 ;* any answer goes back; the answer itself is not used
   call $tk_open('tool.dict', '', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      done = 1
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('again', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)            ;* S.97 stage 2: the new context has no AI line yet; the account may have changed it in the command
   gosub declare.layout                                                ;* the new context is laid out for the window as it is now (it may have been resized in the command)
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub reread
   if pi = 2 then
      for q = 1 to nis
         if iids<ishown<q>> = keep then ci = q
      next q
   end
   if pi = 3 then
      for q = 1 to nx
         if upcase(xnames<q>) = upcase(keep) then cx = q
      next q
   end
   gosub draw.all
   msg = 'back from ' : sent
   return

* E: the item in the IDE (S.88 stage C; it was SED).  The IDE asks for no confirmation of its own; it locks the record while it is open, its save is the dictionary write the kernel's dict-edit rule guards, and the IDE asks the kernel itself
do.edit:
   if nis < 1 then return
